  "system_prompt": "You are a helpful assistant",
  "user_prompt": "Localize the clearly visible objects in this image. Include storage racks/shelving, pallets, boxes/crates, wire containers, transport vehicles such as forklifts or pallet trucks, and other major objects when visible, not only people. Do not invent objects or hidden extents. Separate a support structure and the goods it holds when their visible bounds can be located.\n\nReturn only one JSON object with exactly this structure: {\"objects\": [{\"id\": 1, \"label\": \"object name\", \"bbox\": [x1, y1, x2, y2]}]}.\n\nEach id must be unique. bbox is an axis-aligned rectangle in ORIGINAL IMAGE PIXELS: top-left x1,y1 and bottom-right x2,y2, with origin at the top left of the original image. Use the supplied original width and height. Do NOT use normalized 0-to-1 or 0-to-1000 coordinates. Do not output coordinates in a resized internal image space. Do not add descriptions, explanations, markdown, confidence scores or other fields.\n\nOnly provide a box if you can reliably determine its visible location and extent. Omit objects whose coordinates you cannot determine reliably. If none can be located, return {\"objects\": []}. Do not replace uncertainty with a guessed box.\n\nOriginal image dimensions: width=1280 pixels, height=800 pixels. Use only this image. Coordinates must satisfy 0 <= x1 < x2 <= 1280 and 0 <= y1 < y2 <= 800.",
